  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Lockheed Martin recorded $14.1B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Lockheed Martin received 176 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $80.4M. Lockheed Martin obligations are up 35.6% year over year. Historical totals show fluctuations across recent fiscal years: FY21 $4.7B, FY22 $7.1B, FY23 $8.7B, FY24 $7.2B, FY25 $10.4B, and FY26 $14.1B. The FY2026 to date total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure. Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the dominant market for Lockheed Martin in FY2026 to date, with $12.9B obligated there. Additional NAICS markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $852M, Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services at $115M, and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $97.5M. The largest markets and the award counts show Lockheed Martin focusing its federal sales on missile, space, and aircraft systems while continuing to receive significant individual awards near the reported average award size.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the size and recent trend of Lockheed Martin's federal obligations?",
        "body": "Lockheed Martin has $14.1B in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Lockheed Martin received 176 awards in the period, averaging $80.4M per award, and obligations are up 35.6% year over year. Lockheed Martin obligations rose from FY25 $10.4B to FY26 $14.1B. Lockheed Martin historical yearly totals show FY21 $4.7B, FY22 $7.1B, FY23 $8.7B, and FY24 $7.2B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Lockheed Martin's top markets and product areas this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing is the largest market with $12.9B in obligations for FY2026 to date. Lockheed Martin also has $852M in Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing and $115M in Process, Physical Distribution, and Logistics Consulting Services. Additional markets include All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services at $97.5M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $75.5M."
      }
